      "writtenOn": "2023-02-23T03:09:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then I think this is a bug (perhaps in) perfetto, and it should not call Stop() if Start() failed.\n\nCurrently, if the 1st Start() fails, then the 2nd Start() is a no-op that returns success, even though stuff wasn\u0027t actually *ever* initialized.\n\nWe can\u0027t claim any of this supports concurrency until something is done about this.",
      "parentUuid": "db2887c8_7eef0369",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 135,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 135,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "b6140a4f21afe3d8554edcde3c6996230280efda",
